#====================================================================
# DRAFT-fastnetmon-packet-capture-gating.kv
#====================================================================
id:                     E334
title:                  Gate Linux packet-capture backends for first-pass OHOS network daemons
trigger_tool:           cmake|conan|cc
phase:                  configuration|compilation|testing
error_signature:        if_packet.h|if_xdp.h|bpf|libpcap|libbpf|AF_PACKET|AF_XDP
severity:               3
category:               syscall, network, dependency-closure
match_keywords:         fastnetmon, AF_PACKET, AF_XDP, libbpf, libpcap, netmap, sflow, netflow, DDoS
root_cause:             Network monitoring daemons often bind to Linux packet capture APIs and optional
                        telemetry/control stacks that are not portable to the first OHOS packaging pass.
                        Enabling all collectors at once expands the dependency closure and makes CI
                        failures hard to isolate.
affected_scope:         Packet capture, DDoS monitoring, traffic analytics, and network daemon packages.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/f/fastnetmon/1.2.9

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           feature-gate-private-network-backends
rec_description:        Start with protocol parsers and daemon core that can be built without Linux-only
                        capture backends, then explicitly disable AF_PACKET, AF_XDP/libbpf, Netmap,
                        libpcap mirror capture, plugin runners, and heavyweight API/database closures.
                        Add a consumer smoke test for installed CLI/help behavior, and document which
                        packet paths need real-device validation before enabling them.
rec_command:            -DENABLE_AFPACKET_SUPPORT=OFF -DENABLE_AF_XDP_SUPPORT=OFF -DENABLE_PCAP_SUPPORT=OFF
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               cmake-options-and-notes

forbid_1_pattern:       silently build host-only packet capture backend in an OHOS cross package
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:
doc_file: doc/E334.md

principles: 
last_updated:           2026-07-21

authors: asp1r1n1 <912802346@qq.com>
